attn2-kvarn-verify-shared: one program per (request, kv head, split) for KVarN's uniform verify (mode E).

Research experiment for attn-2 (docs/research/deepinfer/attention-kv.md; gate opened by
gpu-results/e-profile.md: _kvarn_fused_decode_stage1 7.3 ms/layer at 170k, ~40x its DRAM floor).
NOT in patches/series. Written against the image's installed (already patched) vLLM 0.31.0,
whose KVarN modules equal kvarn/files/ (md5 c3a8bddd... / a9b4508e...).

The stock verify path runs the per-token kernel: one program per (query TOKEN, kv head, split),
so at QLEN=8 each int4 tile is dequantized 8 times, and each tl.dot has 8 real-or-padded rows
padded to the MMA's 16, on the tf32 MMA (F16 off). Adds _kvarn_verify_shared_stage1/_stage2:
one program per (REQUEST, kv head, split) dequantizes each chunk once for all QLEN x Q_PER_KV
rows (48 at E, packed densely into a 64-row tile) on fp16-operand MMAs with fp32 accumulate.
Unlike the older KVARN_SHARED_VERIFY kernel (left untouched): any QLEN, no early return (padded
requests write empty partials instead of leaving stage-2 scratch uninitialized), a fixed
spill-free launch config instead of the warmup-shape autotune, a runtime split count.

All knobs are read at import and default off; with KVARN_VERIFY_SHARED unset no new kernel is
compiled or launched and every existing path is unchanged.
  KVARN_VERIFY_SHARED=1           route uniform-QLEN verify batches (QLEN >= 2) to the new kernel:
                                  kvarn_verify_attention's spec-as-decode path, and the eager
                                  _fused_verify_path when its batch is uniform and causal
  KVARN_VERIFY_SHARED_PV16=1      P@V on the fp16-accumulate MMA, per <= 64-token chunk (lossy, tiny)
  KVARN_VERIFY_SHARED_SPLITS=N    KV splits (default ceil(2 * SMs / (B * Hk)): 41 at B=1 on a 3090)
  KVARN_VERIFY_SHARED_CFG=BN,W,S  BLOCK_N, num_warps, num_stages (default 32,8,1)
The boot warmup (_warm_decode_kernels) compiles the new kernels before graph capture when the
route is on. Checks: bench/test_kvarn_verify.py, bench/kvarn_verify_bench.py.

